"# aos-feedback: say what was hard\n\nRecord what was hard about a command or tool, and score how comfortable it is for AIs. Feedback never changes the target. The store is `$AOS_FEEDBACK` (default: the repo's `proto8/feedback/`).\n\n```sh\naos-feedback add \"aos-agent ctl add\" \"usage unclear\" \"show an example\" --kind help --score 0.4 --by opus --model claude-opus\n# aos-feedback: recorded .../aos-agent.jsonl\naos-feedback ls                    # aos-agent  2  2026-11-11T03:18:53.119Z\naos-feedback show aos-agent\naos-feedback score aos-agent --observed ledger.jsonl\n```\n\nThe key is the first word's basename (`aos-agent ctl add` -> `aos-agent`). `--kind` is usage, help, errors, args or other; `--score` is 0 to 1 (1 = comfortable). Flags may go before or after the arguments. `score` prints JSON: the mean scores per kind times calls/(calls+errors+retries) from the `--observed` ledgers. A missing ledger = `FileMissing`; a broken store file = `FileBad`. Inside aos the tool is `lib/aos/feedback` (not in the default packs).\n"
